Current Version can be found [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Ralsei here]. 

Ralsei, added in '''Beta 30.0 '''as a 2/7 for 6G monster, was first nerfed in '''Beta 32.0''' by increasing his cost to 7G. '''Beta 35.0''' followed with decreasing his HP to 5. His effects consisted of a Support effect that would give the attacking monster Ranged. He also had a Dust that would remove Ranged from all ally monsters. 

'''Beta 47.0''' removed Ranged, and as such, this was redesigned. Now, as a 3/3 for 8G, he summons a non-DT monster of your choice directly from your hand, much like a self-use [https://undercards.fandom.com/wiki/Receptionist_3 Receptionist 3]. However, when your next turn starts and Ralsei still lives, that monster returns to your hand (even if it already died, thus moving it from your dustpile). '''Beta 51.1''' gave him +1/+1 and -1 cost and removed his Turn start effect. His Magic also summons a copy rather than the original one. However, the copy will have its stats set to 3/3. '''Beta 52.1''' returned his cost to 8G, but also have him another +1 ATK.

